{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>And you shall dispossess, etc., and you shall dwell, etc.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained that the commandment is ״and you shall dispossess,״ but ״and you shall dwell״ is a promise. And Ramban, of blessed memory, explained that the commandment is ״and you shall dwell,״ and from here they relied to say (Ketubot 110b) that all are encouraged to go up to the Land of Israel." "<b>And it appears</b> that the plain sense of the verse follows Rashi's words, from the fact that Scripture concluded by saying <b>for to you</b>, etc., <b>to possess it</b>; and if dwelling were the commandment, it should have attached this reason to the essence of the commandment and said ״for to you, etc., to dwell in it.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:07.392288890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}